First mistake - until you get quite expert, make sure you are *never* 
burdened or worse. That makes you slower, and a slow adventurer can become 
a dead adventurer very quickly.

AC -2 is also a little high for a level 10 adventurer.

St:17 is quite low for a Valk - have you been eating poisonous corpses? 
These should be avoided until you have a way to cure its effects or are 
poison resistant.

> Your inventory
>    Amulets
>    l - an uncursed amulet of life saving
>    Weapons
>    a - a +1 long sword (weapon in hand)
You really want to have found something better by level 10. You can 
sacrifice for Mjollnir, or as a lawful, you can dip your longsword in 
fountains to try and get it transformed into another artifact.

>    b - a +0 dagger
>    h - a +0 short sword
>    Armor
